<p>Yemen’s coast guard said unidentified armed men boarded the tanker M/T EUREKA off Shabwa province on Saturday, took control of it and steered it through the Gulf of Aden toward Somalia. The coast guard is aligned with Yemen’s internationally recognized government. Reports described the incident as the second oil tanker hijacking in the area in 10 days and at least the fourth vessel hijacking near Somalia in recent weeks.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/TYQ4LBS9nphw_zk09wm6IK3Hfizp3gn5plnt6hwndTT_HX51-KTjFybwxYM-Ef3fbAAwO_nH0F9--7YqK1RpLjhgKiQDqeGEDKLZDYOR5fXDeSnQaEDs6aQWBx9d5Z7lq4uXlbwCUpwm5svVMl5xr9uNlnmvmS_FVmgIqSaX1HRYS2g8w52Kp9lBkc87F9mBjafj80joqIyJCrCUssNc9FO4JxQS8Q' alt='Maritime police forces from Somalia’s semiautonomous Puntland region patrolling the Gulf of Aden last year.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Vessel size: One report said the EUREKA is 88 meters long.</li><li>Ownership: The Yemeni coast guard statement cited by Middle East Monitor did not specify the ship’s ownership.</li><li>Route context: Digi24 reported that the shipowner was seeking an alternative route because of the Strait of Hormuz blockade.</li><li>Earlier tanker: Greek public broadcaster ERT identified the previous tanker in the recent sequence as Honor 25.</li></ul><blockquote>The location of the tanker has been determined, and work is under way to monitor it and take the necessary measures in an attempt to recover it and ensure the safety of its crew - Yemeni coast guard</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Yemeni coast guard: The coast guard said it acted immediately after receiving the report and was coordinating with partners as it pursued the case. (<a href='https://www.middleeastmonitor.com/20260502-oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-taken-toward-somalia-coast-guard/'>Middle East Monitor</a>)</li><li>Somali security officials: Their account, reported by the BBC, identified the attackers as Somali pirates, not unidentified armed men. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpwprl0v2npo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>The New York Times: The newspaper described the hijacking as a sign that piracy risks could overlap with the wider Iran-war security crisis around Yemen and the Houthis. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/02/world/middleeast/hijacking-tanker-houthis-somalia-pirates.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Maritime security monitors: They issued operational warnings for ships in the region but did not attribute responsibility for the EUREKA boarding. (<a href='https://kurier.at/politik/ausland/oeltanker-vor-jemens-kueste-entfuehrt-vae/403156361'>Kurier</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-coast-directed-towards-somalia-11440916#publisher=newsstand'>Oil Tanker Hijacked Off Yemen Coast, Directed Towards Somalia</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/02/world/middleeast/hijacking-tanker-houthis-somalia-pirates.html'>Oil Tanker Hijacking Stokes Fear of Links Between Houthi Rebels and Somali Pirates</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/2/yemen-reports-hijacked-oil-tanker-headed-for-somalia'>Yemen reports hijacked oil tanker headed for Somalia</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cpwprl0v2npo'>Oil tanker hijacked off coast of Yemen and taken towards Somalia</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://jordantimes.com/article/10877805/region/oil-tanker-hijacked-off-yemen-diverted-towards-somalia-yemen-coast-guard'>Oil tanker hijacked off Yemen, diverted towards Somalia — Yemen coast guard</a> - jordantimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rte.ie/news/world/2026/0502/1571488-oil-tanker-yemen/'>Oil tanker hijacked off Yemen, diverted towards Somalia</a> - rte.ie</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458003/oil-tanker-seized-off-yemen-now-headed-towards-somalia'>Oil tanker seized off Yemen, now headed towards Somalia</a> - aaj.tv</li><li><a href='https://w